--TEST--
A `Cell::rich` run whose style sets a field outside the font throws `LogicError` naming the field and the run, and an empty list of runs throws: rule:core-classes/spreadsheet-roster
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Cell;
use Novis\Spreadsheet\Style;

var $fonts = Style::of({ font: 'Arial', size: 12.0, bold: true, italic: true, strike: true, underline: 'double', color: '#336699' });
echo Core\Arr::count(Cell::rich([{ text: 'a', style: $fonts }, { text: 'b' }])->runs ?? []), " runs take every font field\n";

try {
    Cell::rich([{ text: 'a' }, { text: 'b', style: Style::of({ bold: true, fill: '#FFFF00' }) }]);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Cell::rich([{ text: 'a', style: Style::of({ format: 'money' }) }]);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Cell::rich([]);
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
2 runs take every font field
Part 2 of `Cell::rich` has a style with `fill`. A part can only set font fields: `font`, `size`, `bold`, `italic`, `strike`, `underline` and `color`.
Part 1 of `Cell::rich` has a style with `format`. A part can only set font fields: `font`, `size`, `bold`, `italic`, `strike`, `underline` and `color`.
`Cell::rich` needs at least one part, such as `[{ text: 'Total' }]`.
